<title>USA: Clinton seeks $300 million more in disaster aid.</title>
<headline>Clinton seeks $300 million more in disaster aid.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton has boosted the amount of disaster aid he is seeking from Congress for the flood-ravaged states of North Dakota, South Dakota and Minnesota by $300 million, the White House said Thursday.</p>
<p>White House spokesman Mike McCurry told reporters the money brings to $788 million the amount Clinton is seeking for the region, which he visited on Tuesday to see the damage wrought by heavy flooding.</p>
</text>
